Package: sparky-ca
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ca-certificates,
         kwallet6,
         libnss3-tools,
         polkitd,
         qml6-module-org-kde-kcmutils,
         qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
         qml6-module-org-kde-ki18n,
         qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
         qml6-module-qtquick-templates,
         qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: gpgsm,
            libccid,
            opensc,
            openssl-provider-ed521,
            p11-kit,
            pcscd
Suggests: kleopatra,
          okular
Description: ICP-Brasil certificates, browser trust and personal certificates
 Sparky CA installs the certificate authorities of Brazil's ICP-Brasil in the
 system, in Waterfox, Firefox and Chromium, and in GnuPG for Kleopatra, and
 keeps the groups you chose current. It shows every certificate with its
 issuer, expiry and state, imports your A1 certificate, registers your A3
 token, and works on a plain text console as well as in KDE.
 .
 Every download is checked against ITI's published hash and pinned roots, and
 certificates revoked by their authority are never installed. A daily timer
 keeps your chosen groups current and can be turned off.

Package: openssl-provider-ed521
Architecture: amd64
Depends: openssl,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Ed521 signature verification for OpenSSL (ICP-Brasil v7)
 An OpenSSL 3 provider that verifies EdDSA signatures over the curve E-521
 (Ed521, OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.44588.2.1), the algorithm of ICP-Brasil's root
 certificate v7, following Pedro F. Albanese's e521 reference.
 .
 It only verifies: it cannot create keys or sign, and it answers for Ed521
 alone. Installing it adds the provider to OpenSSL's system configuration
 beside the default provider, after checking that the result works, so that
 openssl and the programs that use OpenSSL validate v7 certificates, CRLs
 and CMS signatures. Removing it restores the previous configuration.
